 are revived. ...\\\"\\n- \\\"task_stop\\\": \\\"Stop a background task by its ID. Running agents and shells are cancelled; paused recovered agents are abandoned without resuming them.\\\"\\n- \\\"web_fetch\\\": \\\"Fetches content from a specified URL and processes it using an AI model\\\"\\n- \\\"zoom_image\\\": \\\"Crops a region from a full-resolution static image and returns a magnified view. Coordinates are integers normalized from 0 to 1000 against the displayed ima...\\\"\\n</system-reminder>\"},{\"text\":\"<system-reminder>\\nThe current date is: Thursday, October 1, 2026. Note: This is the authoritative current date — it may differ from the \\\"Today's date\\\" mentioned earlier in the conversation startup context.\\n</system-reminder>\"},{\"text\":\"Use the monitor tool to watch this command: for i in 1 2 3; do echo \\\"EVENT_$i\\\"; sleep 0.3; done. Set description to \\\"test events\\\". After starting the monitor, just say \\\"Monitor launched.\\\"\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"text\":\"The user wants me to use the monitor tool to watch a command. Let me do that.\\n\\nThe monitor tool is available directly in my tool list. Let me call it.\\n\\nThe instruction says: \\\"After starting the monitor, just say 'Monitor launched.'\\\"\\n\\nSo I should call monitor with the command and description \\\"test events\\\".\\n\\nLet me state briefly what I'm doing before the tool call.\\n\\nNote the working directory is /root/verify/pr13005/wt/.integration-tests/1790859733845/monitor-tool-call-3771566. The command should run in the project root by default, which is fine.\\n\\nLet me call the monitor tool.\\n[Thought: true]\"},{\"text\":\"Starting a monitor on the event-emitting command.\\n\\n\"},{\"functionCall\":{\"id\":\"call_b86bb465589f4452a058de27\",\"name\":\"monitor\",\"args\":{\"command\":\"for i in 1 2 3; do echo \\\"EVENT_$i\\\"; sleep 0.3; done\",\"description\":\"test events\"}}}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"parts\":[{\"functionResponse\":{\"id\":\"c