all_b86bb465589f4452a058de27\",\"name\":\"monitor\",\"response\":{\"output\":\"Monitor started.\\nid: mon_f202cc55ea6e4eab\\ncommand: for i in 1 2 3; do echo \\\"EVENT_$i\\\"; sleep 0.3; done\\ndescription: test events\\nmax_events: 1000\\nidle_timeout: 300000ms\\nEvents will be delivered as notifications. The monitor auto-stops after 1000 events or 300000ms of silence.\\nTo inspect: /tasks (text) or the interactive Background tasks dialog (focus the footer Background tasks pill, then Enter — detail view + live updates).\"}}}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"text\":\"The monitor was started. Now I should just say \\\"Monitor launched.\\\"\\n\\nThe user said: \\\"After starting the monitor, just say 'Monitor launched.'\\\"\\n\\nSo my response should be minimal.\\n[Thought: true]\"},{\"text\":\"Monitor launched.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"parts\":[{\"text\":\"<task-notification>\\n<task-id>mon_f202cc55ea6e4eab</task-id>\\n<tool-use-id>call_b86bb465589f4452a058de27</tool-use-id>\\n<kind>monitor</kind>\\n<status>running</status>\\n<event-count>1</event-count>\\n<summary>Monitor \\\"test events\\\" emitted event #1.</summary>\\n<result>EVENT_1</result>\\n</task-notification>\\n\\n<task-notification>\\n<task-id>mon_f202cc55ea6e4eab</task-id>\\n<tool-use-id>call_b86bb465589f4452a058de27</tool-use-id>\\n<kind>monitor</kind>\\n<status>running</status>\\n<event-count>2</event-count>\\n<summary>Monitor \\\"test events\\\" emitted event #2.</summary>\\n<result>EVENT_2</result>\\n</task-notification>\\n\\n<task-notification>\\n<task-id>mon_f202cc55ea6e4eab</task-id>\\n<tool-use-id>call_b86bb465589f4452a058de27</tool-use-id>\\n<kind>monitor</kind>\\n<status>running</status>\\n<event-count>3</event-count>\\n<summary>Monitor \\\"test events\\\" emitted event #3.</summary>\\n<result>EVENT_3</result>\\n</task-notification>\\n\\n<task-notification>\\n<task-id>mon_f202cc55ea6e4eab</task-id>\\n<tool-use-id>call_b86bb465589f4452a058de27</tool-use-id>\\n<kind>monitor</kind>\\n<status>co